    {
      "$comment": "P1 player heads: the modular outfits ship their own body geometry (bodyCut keeps head+neck of the fused base; the seam hides in every collar). The pack's Godot-UE export references two textures that do not exist (typo'd `_png.png` names) and defaults to the Dark basecolor variants — the runtime skin-tint model multiplies DOWN from the Light variants (packages/shared appearance.ts), so both are overridden. `null` drops the broken slot.",
      "pack": "quaternius-base-characters",
      "category": "characters",
      "glob": "Base Characters/Godot - UE/Superhero_*_FullBody.gltf",
      "skinned": true,
      "bodyCut": {
        "meshPattern": "Superhero|Retopology",
        "bones": ["Head", "neck_01"],
        "threshold": 0.4
      },
      "imageOverrides": {
        "T_Hair_1_Normal_png.png": null,
        "T_Eye_Normal_png.png": null,
        "T_Superhero_Male_Dark.png": "../Textures/T_Superhero_Male_Ligh.png",
        "T_Superhero_Female_Dark_BaseColor.png": "../Textures/T_Superhero_Female_Light_BaseColor.png",
        "T_Hair_1_BaseColor.png": {
          "grayscale": true,
          "multiplyRGB": [1.47, 1.47, 1.47]
        },
        "T_Hair_2_BaseColor.png": {
          "grayscale": true,
          "multiplyRGB": [1.47, 1.47, 1.47]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "$comment": "Hairstyles + beard, skinned to the shared 65-bone rig (head bone variant). Eyebrows_* are deliberately excluded — the base bodies ship eyebrows built in. Hair basecolors bake to a brightness-normalized luminance map (grayscale mean 0.56 × 1.47 ≈ 0.82) so runtime multiply tints land on the picked swatch with strand shading intact.",
      "pack": "quaternius-base-characters",
      "category": "characters",
      "glob": "Hairstyles/Rigged to Head Bone/glTF (Godot -Unreal)/Hair_*.gltf",
      "skinned": true,
      "imageOverrides": {
        "T_Hair_1_BaseColor.png": {
          "grayscale": true,
          "multiplyRGB": [1.47, 1.47, 1.47]
        },
        "T_Hair_2_BaseColor.png": {
          "grayscale": true,
          "multiplyRGB": [1.47, 1.47, 1.47]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "$comment": "Outfits are full bodies below the neck, incl. their own exposed-skin geometry (MI_Regular_* materials). The pack only ships the Dark skin variant; multiplyRGB lifts it to the Light superhero tone the faces use (per-channel light/dark means measured with sharp), so one runtime skin tint lands on the same color for face and hands.",
      "pack": "quaternius-outfits-fantasy",
      "category": "characters",
      "glob": "Exports/glTF (Godot-Unreal)/Outfits/*_*.gltf",
      "skinned": true,
      "imageOverrides": {
        "T_Regular_Male_Dark_BaseColor.png": {
          "multiplyRGB": [1.062, 1.094, 1.13]
        },
        "T_Regular_Female_Dark_BaseColor.png": {
          "multiplyRGB": [1.036, 1.055, 1.078]
        }
      }
    },
